In `data_is_empty`:
- `p` points to `' '` (the space after abstract name)
- `while (*p == ' ') p++;` → `p` points to `'$'`
- `*p == '$'`, so `p++` → `p` points to `'\0'`
- `parse_special` is called with `p` pointing to `'\0'`
- In `parse_special`: `**cmd == '\0'`, so it returns NULL immediately
- Back in `data_is_empty`: `p++` → `p` points past the end of the string!
